# This project's real environment variables live in two places, one per
# service (each already has its own .env.example with the full details):
#
#   backend/.env.example   -> GOOGLE_API_KEY, GEMINI_MODEL, CORS_ORIGINS, PORT
#   frontend/.env.example  -> VITE_API_URL
#
# Copy each to backend/.env and frontend/.env respectively and fill in your
# values. This root-level file exists only as a map to those two — nothing
# reads a root-level .env directly.
#
# docker-compose.yml reads backend/.env via env_file, and bakes
# VITE_API_URL into the frontend image at build time via --build-arg (see
# docker-compose.yml and README.md).
